speechtext:
For a statement showing each and every treaty or convention made by the government of the United Kingdom with any foreign state, now outstanding and in effect in whole or ft part, which in terms applies to the Dominion of Canada, or which the parliament of Canada has confirmed by statute or by resolution, or to which, in whole or in part, the government of Canada has given its formal adhesion; giving the date of each such treaty or convention, the name of foreign state with which such treaty or convention was concluded, and citing the references to the publication of each such treaty or convention;
2.	For a similar statement showing each and every treaty or convention made or concluded by Canada with any foreign state, citing similar references to the publication of each such treaty or convention; and
3.	For a statement showing each and every enactment of the parliament of Great Britain, which, by its express terms or by necessary implication applies to the Dominion of Canada.
